  "conclusion": {
    "counter_arm": "The KV-traffic counter is a function of position arithmetic alone. It has zero discrimination against a wrong index score at every context, including the 200,000 and 1,000,000 the headline ratios are quoted at.",
    "token_arm": "End-to-end token agreement can only see a wrong index score from the first prompt length at which a ranking layer discards a candidate. Below it the selected set is the whole candidate set and ROUTE.INDEX_TOPK emits it sorted ascending, so neither membership nor order carries score information."
